            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "cjwystz"
            },
            "body": "Hi @OrangeRedeng, thank you for referencing this PR in #44525 and for your work on Ascend TP MoE optimizations.\n\nThis PR specifically fixes the Ascend/NPU path in `AscendTPDispatcher.dispatch()`, keeping routing weights in FP32 instead of casting them to the hidden-state dtype. I noticed that #44525 currently includes the same change. Its earlier description listed #42182 as covering non-Ascend paths, so I wanted to point out that the two changes overlap in the Ascend dispatcher.\n\nWould you and the relevant reviewers consider reviewing this small correctness fix separately and landing it before the broader optimizations? This PR includes numerical validation on Ascend 910B3, and #44525 could then build on the fix. I am happy to provide additional validation or address any feedback.\n\nI have also updated the title to follow the current PR title format. Thank you for your time and guidance!\n",
