    "body": "Closes #39351\r\n\r\nSupersedes #39369 and #39394 (same one-line fix): #39369 could not run its\r\ntest or validate on NPU hardware; #39394's CI is failing. This PR adds\r\nreal-hardware numerical validation on 910B3. If maintainers prefer to land\r\nvia #39369 with this evidence appended, I'm happy to close this one.\r\n\r\n## What\r\n`AscendTPDispatcher.dispatch()` downcasts the FP32 routing weights produced by\r\nthe TopK layer to the hidden-state dtype before they reach\r\n`npu_moe_finalize_routing`. The finalize kernel natively accepts FP32 scales,\r\nso the cast discards precision in every MoE layer on the default NPU path\r\n(`a2a_backend.is_none() and is_npu()` -> AscendTPDispatcher).\r\n\r\nThis keeps routing weights in FP32 through dispatch/combine.\r\n\r\n## Evidence (910B3, CANN 9.0.0, torch_npu 2.10.0, sglang v0.5.18)\r\nAgainst an FP64 reference recomputation of the finalize semantics\r\n(256x512 hidden, 16 experts, top-8, drop_pad_mode=2):\r\n\r\n| path | max abs err vs FP64 ref |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| kernel with FP32 weights | 4.0e-07 |\r\n| kernel with BF16 weights (current) | 1.6e-02 |\r\n| pure-math BF16 weights | 8.0e-03 |\r\n\r\nQuantized paths (INT8/MXFP8) are untouched: the change only affects routing\r\nweights; hidden-state quant mode is selected separately via\r\n`ascend_dispatcher_output_dtype`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39019272761](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39019272761)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39019272756](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39019272756)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39019272747](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39019272747)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
