  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Hi @HaiShaw @Edwardf0t1, this is a small NPU-side fix for MoE routing precision in AscendTPDispatcher (keep routing weights in FP32 to match eager-mode numerics). Could you help add the `run-ci` label so CI can run? Happy to address any comments. Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-06T14:50:31Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/42182#issuecomment-6018881498",
      "id": 6018881498,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-06T14:50:31Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "cjwystz"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "<!-- pr-check-comment runs=39019270557 -->\nRequired checks failed on 2d16556; this PR cannot be merged until they pass.\n\n**PR title** ([run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39019270557))\n> PR title must use \"[Type] scope: title\" or \"[Type] [Hardware] scope: title\". Type must be one of: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, Chore. Scope is required and may be any module or model name, with unrestricted letter case (letters, numbers, dots, underscores, slashes, or hyphens). Hardware is optional; use a single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend. Reverts must use GitHub's default format: Revert \"original title\". Use one space between fields and after the colon, with a non-empty title and no leading or trailing whitespace. Examples: \"[Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing\", \"[Feat] qwen3: Add model support\", \"[Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance\".\nEdit the title; the check reruns on its own.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T09:00:31Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/42182#issuecomment-6232039657",
      "id": 6232039657,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-17T09:20:34Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "github-actions[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @OrangeRedeng, thank you for referencing this PR in #44525 and for your work on Ascend TP MoE optimizations.\n\nThis PR specifically fixes the Ascend/NPU path in `AscendTPDispatcher.dispatch()`, keeping routing weights in FP32 instead of casting them to the hidden-state dtype. I noticed that #44525 currently includes the same change. Its earlier description listed #42182 as covering non-Ascend paths, so I wanted to point out that the two changes overlap in the Ascend dispatcher.\n\nWould you and the relevant reviewers consider reviewing this small correctness fix separately and landing it before the broader optimizations? This PR includes numerical validation on Ascend 910B3, and #44525 could then build on the fix. I am happy to provide additional validation or address any feedback.\n\nI have also updated the title to follow the current PR title format. Thank you for your time and guidance!\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T09:20:18Z",
